        "title": "fix(discord): strip attachments >10MB before send to prevent HTTP 413 silent message loss (fixes #99021)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #99021.\n\n## Changes Made\n\n1. send.outbound.ts: DEFAULT=10MB (Discord bot limit). Explicit mediaMaxMb respected.\n2. send.shared.ts: effectiveMaxBytes = maxBytes ?? 10MB\n3. send.receipt.ts: Added mediaStripped flag\n4. 3 regression tests\n\n## Evidence (commit: a718954a46)\n\n### Real Discord API proof (live bot)\nBEFORE: 11MB file -> HTTP 413 -> message lost\nAFTER: Size check -> text delivered, receipt kind: text\n\n### Unit tests (47/47 passed)\n- >10MB default config triggers fallback\n- mediaMaxMb:50 respects config, 15MB file sent normally\n- text-only fallback with long reply\n\n## AI Assistance\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n",
